<!--
  ============================================================================
  SWCPZoomerIcon_Fix.xml                     Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  THE BUG
  =======
  Star Wars KotOR Resources and Materials (guy762.MM.KotORCore, WS 3254370945)
  ships SWCP_Core.dll referencing a Unity AssetBundle that was never packaged:

      <mod>\SWCP-UnityAssets\Materials\StandaloneWindows64\SWCPshaders

  Absent from the Workshop upload AND the GitHub repo. Filed upstream as issue
  #7 (open). Every launch produces:

      Could not execute post-long-event action. Exception: NullReferenceException
        at Verse.BuildableDef.ResolveIcon () [0x00081]
        at Verse.ThingDef.ResolveIcon ()
        at Verse.BuildableDef.<PostLoad>b__78_0 ()
        at Verse.LongEventHandler.ExecuteToExecuteWhenFinished ()

  SEVERITY, CORRECTED  [VERIFIED FROM IL 2026-08-10]
  ==================================================
  Our notes used to call this severity-2 on the belief that a throw here aborts
  the rest of RimWorld's post-load queue. THAT IS FALSE. The method wraps each
  queued action in its own try/catch (18-byte try around one Action::Invoke; the
  handler's leave targets the loop INCREMENT). One failed action costs exactly
  that action. See mods/benign_log_errors.md section 6 for the full evidence.

  So this patch is cosmetic hygiene, not a rescue. It is worth shipping anyway:
  the error is a red Log.Error that pops the debug window every single launch,
  and noise that everyone learns to ignore is how real errors get missed.

  ROOT CAUSE, TRACED TO ONE DEF  [VERIFIED FROM IL 2026-08-10]
  ============================================================
  Exactly one def is responsible, and it is the only consumer in the entire
  Workshop tree:

      SWCP_VATS_Zoomer   in  3254370945/1.6/Defs/Thing_VATS_Zoomer.xml

  Its graphicClass is SWCP.Core.VATS.Graphic_Zoomer, whose MatAt() is a
  one-liner returning the static field SWCP.Core.Unity.Materials::ZoomMat with
  no null guard. When the bundle fails to open, LoadMaterial returns null and
  ZoomMat is a real C# null. Vanilla BuildableDef.ResolveIcon then does:

      IL_007B  callvirt Verse.Graphic::MatAt
      IL_0080  stloc.3                       <- Material mat, null
      IL_0081  ldloc.3                       <- the reported offset
      IL_0082  callvirt UnityEngine.Material::get_shader   <- NRE

  Note the chain is self-triggering: ResolveIcon touches ZoomMat, which is the
  first access to Materials, whose [StaticConstructorOnStartup] cctor then
  attempts the bundle load. That is why the "Bundle Path" lines appear
  immediately before the NRE rather than at some unrelated point in startup.

  THE FIX
  =======
  Give the def a uiIconPath. Vanilla BuildableDef.<PostLoad>b__78_0 checks it
  FIRST and skips ResolveIcon entirely when it is non-empty:

      IL_0000  ldfld  BuildableDef::uiIconPath
      IL_0006  call   GenText::NullOrEmpty
      IL_000B  brtrue.s  -> IL_0021          ; empty  -> ResolveIcon
      IL_000D  ...      uiIcon = ContentFinder<Texture2D>.Get(uiIconPath, true)
      IL_001F  br.s      -> IL_0027          ; non-empty -> ResolveIcon SKIPPED

  That lambda is the ONLY caller of ResolveIcon in Assembly-CSharp (TerrainDef
  and ThingDef merely chain to the base), so a non-empty uiIconPath makes the
  NRE structurally unreachable rather than merely unlikely.

  512blank is the texture the def already uses for graphicData/texPath, and
  Textures/512blank.png really exists in the SWCP mod, so ContentFinder resolves
  it cleanly with no new error.

  WHY NOT THE OTHER OPTIONS
  =========================
    * Turning off the EnableZoom mod setting: DOES NOT WORK. Verified: the
      bundle load lives in two [StaticConstructorOnStartup] cctors (Materials,
      Shaders) that read no settings at all. EnableZoom is only read by
      JobDriver_AttackHybrid at attack time.
    * Replacing graphicClass with Verse.Graphic_Single: also stops the NRE, but
      JobDriver_AttackHybrid does an unguarded castclass to Graphic_Zoomer, so
      it trades a startup NRE for a mid-combat InvalidCastException.
    * A stub file at the bundle path: AssetBundle.LoadFromFile returns null for
      any unloadable file, so the mod takes the identical branch. It also means
      writing into a Steam Workshop folder, which Steam re-validates and wipes.
    * Disabling SWCP: not an option. It defines 1,959 defs and ships 36
      assemblies, and the whole KotOR family loads after it.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Conditional-wrapped, so if SWCP ships a fix or renames the def this becomes a
  silent no-op. Adds a field the def does not currently have; changes no
  runtime behaviour, since graphicClass is untouched and Graphic_Zoomer is still
  what JobDriver_AttackHybrid casts to.

  EXPECTED AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ============================
    * GONE:    "Could not execute post-long-event action" plus the ResolveIcon
               NRE, and with it the last red error in the load.
    * REMAINS: the two "Bundle Path" / "Failed to load bundle" blocks. They are
               not caused by this def; both cctors still run, just later, from
               StaticConstructorOnStartupUtility.CallAll. Do not read their
               presence as the patch having failed.
    * Confirmed twice-per-launch by IL: two distinct call sites, and the mod
      caches a failed load as null so the guard never trips.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="SWCP_VATS_Zoomer"][not(uiIconPath)]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="SWCP_VATS_Zoomer"][not(uiIconPath)]</xpath>
      <value>
        <uiIconPath>512blank</uiIconPath>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
